WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.758
Yes or No Questions.

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:05.473
Day 3 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.223 --> 00:00:08.247
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.527 --> 00:00:13.625
Today's goal: turn any sentence into a yes or no question, and answer naturally.

5
00:00:13.905 --> 00:00:17.852
These are the most common questions at counters, in shops, and at work.

6
00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:20.055
Part 1.

7
00:00:20.335 --> 00:00:23.173
Rule 1: with am or is or are, swap the order.

8
00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.767
Here is a quick table:

9
00:00:26.047 --> 00:00:27.412
Statement, and Question.

10
00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:28.951
The train is late.:

11
00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:30.447
Is the train late?

12
00:00:30.727 --> 00:00:31.943
You are free today.:

13
00:00:32.223 --> 00:00:33.460
Are you free today?

14
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.020
This seat is taken.:

15
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.559
Is this seat taken?

16
00:00:36.839 --> 00:00:38.012
They were at the meeting.:

17
00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:39.487
Were they at the meeting?

18
00:00:40.837 --> 00:00:41.711
Part 2.

19
00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:45.106
Rule 2: with action verbs, add do or does or did.

20
00:00:46.356 --> 00:00:47.700
Here is a quick table:

21
00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.964
Statement, and Question, and Note.

22
00:00:50.244 --> 00:00:51.652
You like spicy food.

23
00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:52.807
Question:

24
00:00:53.087 --> 00:00:54.601
Do you like spicy food?

25
00:00:54.881 --> 00:00:55.628
Note:

26
00:00:55.908 --> 00:00:57.721
I or you or we or they, then do.

27
00:00:58.001 --> 00:00:59.004
She works here.

28
00:00:59.284 --> 00:01:00.159
Question:

29
00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:01.548
Does she work here?

30
00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.729
Note: he or she or it, then does, verb loses -s.

31
00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:06.076
They delivered it.

32
00:01:06.356 --> 00:01:07.231
Question:

33
00:01:07.511 --> 00:01:08.727
Did they deliver it?

34
00:01:09.007 --> 00:01:11.503
Note: past, then did, verb goes to base.

35
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:13.532
The bus goes to MG Road.

36
00:01:13.812 --> 00:01:14.687
Question:

37
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:16.823
Does the bus go to MG Road?

38
00:01:18.173 --> 00:01:18.919
Warning:

39
00:01:19.199 --> 00:01:20.479
Most common mistake.

40
00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:21.869
Does she works here?

41
00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:24.154
Did you went? then Does she work here?

42
00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:25.351
Did you go?

43
00:01:25.631 --> 00:01:30.858
The do or does or did already shows the tense, so the main verb stays in its base form.

44
00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:33.104
Part 3.

45
00:01:33.384 --> 00:01:37.821
Rule 3: with can or will or should or have (helper verbs), swap the order.

46
00:01:39.071 --> 00:01:40.415
Here is a quick table:

47
00:01:40.695 --> 00:01:42.061
Statement, and Question.

48
00:01:42.341 --> 00:01:43.898
I can pay by UPI.:

49
00:01:44.178 --> 00:01:45.714
Can I pay by UPI?

50
00:01:45.994 --> 00:01:47.551
The shop will open at 10.:

51
00:01:47.831 --> 00:01:49.346
Will the shop open at 10?

52
00:01:49.626 --> 00:01:50.778
We should book early.:

53
00:01:51.058 --> 00:01:52.189
Should we book early?

54
00:01:52.469 --> 00:01:53.535
You have finished.:

55
00:01:53.815 --> 00:01:54.861
Have you finished?

56
00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:56.741
There is a pharmacy nearby.:

57
00:01:57.021 --> 00:01:58.578
Is there a pharmacy nearby?

58
00:01:59.928 --> 00:02:00.845
Part 4.

59
00:02:01.125 --> 00:02:03.003
Answering yes or no questions.

60
00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:05.597
Here is a quick table:

61
00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:09.247
Question, and Short answer (natural), and Full answer (clear).

62
00:02:09.527 --> 00:02:10.871
Is the train on time?

63
00:02:11.151 --> 00:02:12.602
Short answer (natural):

64
00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:15.122
Yes, it is. / No, it isn't.

65
00:02:15.402 --> 00:02:16.789
Full answer (clear):

66
00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.733
No, it's 20 minutes late.

67
00:02:19.013 --> 00:02:20.207
Do you take cards?

68
00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:21.938
Short answer (natural):

69
00:02:22.218 --> 00:02:24.266
Yes, we do. / No, we don't.

70
00:02:24.546 --> 00:02:25.933
Full answer (clear):

71
00:02:26.213 --> 00:02:28.453
Yes, we take all cards and UPI.

72
00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:30.013
Did you get my email?

73
00:02:30.293 --> 00:02:31.743
Short answer (natural):

74
00:02:32.023 --> 00:02:34.242
Yes, I did. / No, I didn't.

75
00:02:34.522 --> 00:02:35.909
Full answer (clear):

76
00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.042
Not yet.

77
00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:38.602
Could you send it again?

78
00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:39.949
Can I sit here?

79
00:02:40.229 --> 00:02:41.679
Short answer (natural):

80
00:02:41.959 --> 00:02:44.882
Sure! / Of course. / Sorry, it's taken.

81
00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:46.549
Full answer (clear):

82
00:02:46.829 --> 00:02:48.557
Sorry, my friend is sitting here.

83
00:02:48.837 --> 00:02:49.775
Have you eaten?

84
00:02:50.055 --> 00:02:51.506
Short answer (natural):

85
00:02:51.786 --> 00:02:53.706
Yes, I have. / Not yet.

86
00:02:53.986 --> 00:02:55.373
Full answer (clear):

87
00:02:55.653 --> 00:02:56.506
Not yet.

88
00:02:56.786 --> 00:02:57.981
Shall we go together?

89
00:02:59.331 --> 00:02:59.971
Tip:

90
00:03:00.251 --> 00:03:04.539
Don't answer with only \Yes\ or \No\.

91
00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:06.589
A bare No. can sound rude.

92
00:03:06.869 --> 00:03:07.787
Add a little:

93
00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:10.520
No, sorry, we don't. or Yes, of course!

94
00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:12.830
Part 5.

95
00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.011
Polite yes or no questions you'll use every day.

96
00:03:17.261 --> 00:03:18.883
Is this the queue for tickets?

97
00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:21.083
Do you have this in a larger size?

98
00:03:21.363 --> 00:03:23.560
Does this bus go to the railway station?

99
00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.184
Can I pay by card?

100
00:03:25.464 --> 00:03:28.301
Is there a lift or washroom or ATM nearby?

101
00:03:28.581 --> 00:03:30.629
Did you get a chance to look at my PR?

102
00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:32.275
Have you booked the tickets?

103
00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:34.969
Are you using this chair?

104
00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:37.257
Part 6.

105
00:03:37.537 --> 00:03:39.628
Conversation: at a medical shop.

106
00:03:40.878 --> 00:03:42.905
Here is how the conversation goes.

107
00:03:43.185 --> 00:03:43.910
Hi.

108
00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.067
Do you have something for a cold?

109
00:03:46.347 --> 00:03:47.457
Yes, we do.

110
00:03:47.737 --> 00:03:49.187
Do you have a fever too?

111
00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:50.598
No, I don't.

112
00:03:50.878 --> 00:03:53.374
Just a runny nose and a sore throat.

113
00:03:53.654 --> 00:03:54.763
Okay.

114
00:03:55.043 --> 00:03:56.963
Is it for you or for a child?

115
00:03:57.243 --> 00:03:58.395
It's for me.

116
00:03:58.675 --> 00:04:01.406
Can I take it with my blood-pressure tablets?

117
00:04:02.756 --> 00:04:04.356
The conversation continues.

118
00:04:04.636 --> 00:04:05.916
Yes, that's fine.

119
00:04:06.196 --> 00:04:07.625
Do you have any allergies?

120
00:04:07.905 --> 00:04:09.036
No, I don't.

121
00:04:09.316 --> 00:04:11.577
Is it okay to take it before food?

122
00:04:11.857 --> 00:04:13.223
Better after food.

123
00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:14.932
Take it twice a day.

124
00:04:15.212 --> 00:04:16.151
Thank you.

125
00:04:16.431 --> 00:04:18.351
Can I pay by UPI?

126
00:04:18.631 --> 00:04:19.335
Sure.

127
00:04:19.615 --> 00:04:21.215
Scan the QR code here.

128
00:04:22.565 --> 00:04:23.503
Part 7.

129
00:04:23.783 --> 00:04:24.701
Practice.

130
00:04:25.951 --> 00:04:26.591
1.

131
